Original commit body from 74f54b8d84321de0a7952a0ac586741067ef40df:

INV-vokog. ADR-0016 section 4's fourth verdict is granted only when opaque
launches are the SOLE remaining blocker -- spelled qualifying_only = not
unknown. But a launch put its own module INTO unknown, so the condition was
unsatisfiable whenever a launch existed and vacuous when none did. The verdict
built on 2026-08-13 for exactly this consumer could never fire on the substrate
it was built for, and no amount of catalogue work would have changed it.

Measured on a live self-survey (154,505 edges, 39,297 production-scoped):
80 of 81 opaque launch sites were also counted as uncatalogued modules.

The one-edge positive control is what makes this a defect rather than a
coverage complaint -- a single bash `id` launch, alone on the substrate:

    unknown = ['id']    opaque = ['id.id']    qualifying_only = False

One edge, both sets, self-cancelling. Two controls discriminate: a python
subprocess.run call alone gives unknown=[] / qualifying_only=True, and a
catalogued builtins.open alone gives complete=True. (Both controls initially
passed for the WRONG reason -- passing every language let the analyzer-blind
check fire first -- and are now scoped to their substrate.)

ONE FACT, TWO HOMES. Two channels know a call is a launch: the catalogue
(declares_opaque_crossing) and the PRODUCER STAMP the bash analyzer sets, which
is the only evidence those edges will ever carry since ADR-0016 rules out a
bash io_primitives catalogue. _opaque_launch_sites reads the stamp FIRST by
design (INV-larol); _uncatalogued_external_modules never asked it. Both now
route through _is_producer_stamped_launch. The python path was immune only
INCIDENTALLY -- subprocess.run carries a row classify_call matches -- so that
accident is pinned by a test rather than left as luck.

Nothing is hidden by the skip: every site it stops counting as blindness is
still NAMED in the caveat, checkable against the source. What changes is which
channel reports it.

Measured: 212 uncatalogued modules -> 137; launch disclosure unchanged at 81.
Reconciled -- of the 80 overlapping, 5 survive (os, subprocess, stat, base64,
coverage) because those names are both a shell command and a module with
independent uncatalogued python calls, which is correct.

THE SELF-PROOF VERDICT DOES NOT MOVE. Still 18/18 inconclusive: the remaining
137 modules still block. Stated so this is not mistaken for a fix for
INV-dabuf.

Suite: 22,879 passed / 7 skipped / 17 xfailed (= 22,903 ingested), 100%
coverage, core passes in isolation, mypy ratchet clean at 672.

